# PixiJS v8 Development Rules & Best Practices

## 🎮 Game Development Architecture

### Core Structure
- **Game.ts**: Main game class, handles Application initialization, coordinates all managers
- **BoardManager.ts**: Manages game grid, node positioning, grid operations
- **Node.ts**: Individual game elements with interactive properties
- **PathTracker.ts**: Handles user input, path validation, match detection
- **RefillManager.ts**: Manages grid refilling, node spawning, chain reactions
- **UIManager.ts**: UI elements, score display, game state indicators

### File Organization
```
src/
├── core/
│   ├── Game.ts              # Main game controller
│   ├── BoardManager.ts      # Grid management
│   ├── Node.ts             # Interactive game elements
│   ├── PathTracker.ts      # Input handling & path logic
│   ├── RefillManager.ts    # Grid refilling & spawning
│   └── UIManager.ts        # UI management
├── systems/                # Additional game systems
├── utils/                  # Helper functions
└── main.ts                # Entry point
```

## 🚀 PixiJS v8 Specific Rules

### Application Initialization
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - PixiJS v8 way
const app = new Application();
await app.init({
    width: 480,
    height: 720,
    backgroundColor: 0x222a36,
    antialias: true,
});
document.body.appendChild(app.canvas);

// ❌ WRONG - Old v7 way
const app = new Application({ width: 480, height: 720 });
document.body.appendChild(app.view);
```

### Canvas Access
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
app.canvas                    // Direct canvas access
app.canvas.style.position = "absolute"
app.canvas.width             // Canvas width
app.canvas.height            // Canvas height

// ❌ WRONG
app.view.canvas              // Not needed in v8
app.view as HTMLCanvasElement // Unnecessary casting
```

### Interactive Events (Event Mode System)
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - PixiJS v8 Event Mode
displayObject.eventMode = "static";     // Non-bubbling events
displayObject.eventMode = "dynamic";    // Bubbling events
displayObject.eventMode = "none";       // No events
displayObject.cursor = "pointer";       // Cursor style

// ❌ WRONG - Old v7 way
displayObject.interactive = true;
displayObject.buttonMode = true;
```

### Event Registration
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Event registration
node.on('pointerdown', () => this.onPointerDown(node));
node.on('pointerover', () => this.onPointerMove(node));
node.on('pointerup', () => this.onPointerUp());

// ✅ CORRECT - Document events for global handling
document.addEventListener('pointerup', () => this.onPointerUp());
```

### Graphics Drawing
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Modern Graphics API
graphics.clear();
graphics.rect(0, 0, width, height);
graphics.fill({ color: 0xff0000, alpha: 1 });

// ✅ CORRECT - Legacy API (still works)
graphics.clear();
graphics.beginFill(0xff0000);
graphics.drawCircle(0, 0, radius);
graphics.endFill();
```

### Text Properties
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Text anchor setting
text.anchor.set(0.5, 0);     // Center horizontally, top vertically
text.anchor.set(0.5, 0.5);   // Center both axes

// ❌ WRONG
text.anchor = { x: 0.5, y: 0 }; // Type error in v8
```

## 🎯 Game Development Patterns

### Manager Pattern
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Manager class structure
export class GameManager {
    private game: Game;
    
    constructor(game: Game) {
        this.game = game;
    }
    
    public update(): void {
        // Update logic
    }
    
    public destroy(): void {
        // Cleanup logic
    }
}
```

### Event-Driven Architecture
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Event handling
export class InputManager {
    private onMatch: (nodes: Node[]) => void = () => {};
    
    public setMatchCallback(callback: (nodes: Node[]) => void): void {
        this.onMatch = callback;
    }
    
    private handleMatch(nodes: Node[]): void {
        this.onMatch(nodes);
    }
}
```

### Node Management
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Node creation with events
export class NodeManager {
    private pathTracker: PathTracker;
    
    createNode(row: number, col: number, color: NodeColor): Node {
        const node = new Node(row, col, color);
        this.pathTracker.registerNodeEvents(node); // Register events immediately
        return node;
    }
}
```

## 🔧 Development Workflow

### 1. Project Setup
```bash
# Initialize new PixiJS v8 project
npm init -y
npm install pixi.js@^8.0.0
npm install -D typescript vite @types/node
```

### 2. TypeScript Configuration
```json
// tsconfig.json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2020",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "strict": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true
  }
}
```

### 3. Vite Configuration
```javascript
// vite.config.js
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';

export default defineConfig({
  build: {
    target: 'esnext',
    rollupOptions: {
      output: {
        format: 'es'
      }
    }
  }
});
```

## 🎨 Best Practices

### Performance
- Use `sortableChildren = true` for z-index management
- Clear graphics before redrawing: `graphics.clear()`
- Remove event listeners on destroy
- Use object pooling for frequently created/destroyed objects

### Memory Management
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Proper cleanup
export class GameObject {
    destroy(): void {
        this.removeAllListeners();
        this.parent?.removeChild(this);
        this.destroy({ children: true });
    }
}
```

### Responsive Design
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Responsive canvas
app.resizeTo = app.canvas;
window.addEventListener('resize', () => {
    // Handle resize logic
});
```

### Debug & Development
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Debug logging
console.log(`Node created: row=${row}, col=${col}, color=${color}`);
console.log(`Pointer down on node:`, node.row, node.col, node.color);
```

## 🚨 Common Pitfalls to Avoid

### 1. Event Mode Confusion
```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Mixing old and new APIs
sprite.interactive = true;  // Old v7
sprite.eventMode = "static"; // New v8 - use this instead
```

### 2. Canvas Access
```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Incorrect canvas access
document.body.appendChild(app.view); // Old v7
// ✅ CORRECT
document.body.appendChild(app.canvas); // New v8
```

### 3. Async Initialization
```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Synchronous initialization
const app = new Application({ width: 480, height: 720 });
// ✅ CORRECT
const app = new Application();
await app.init({ width: 480, height: 720 });
```

### 4. Event Registration for New Objects
```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Forgetting to register events for new objects
const newNode = new Node(row, col, color);
container.addChild(newNode); // Missing event registration!

// ✅ CORRECT
const newNode = new Node(row, col, color);
container.addChild(newNode);
pathTracker.registerNodeEvents(newNode); // Register events!
```

## 📋 Template Checklist

When starting a new PixiJS v8 project:

- [ ] Initialize Application with async init()
- [ ] Set up proper canvas styling
- [ ] Create manager classes for different game systems
- [ ] Implement event-driven architecture
- [ ] Set up proper TypeScript configuration
- [ ] Configure Vite for ES modules
- [ ] Implement proper cleanup and memory management
- [ ] Add debug logging for development
- [ ] Test interactive elements thoroughly
- [ ] Ensure new objects get proper event registration

## 🎯 Quick Start Commands

```bash
# Create new project structure
mkdir my-pixijs-game && cd my-pixijs-game
npm init -y
npm install pixi.js@^8.0.0
npm install -D typescript vite @types/node

# Create basic file structure
mkdir -p src/core src/systems src/utils
touch src/main.ts src/core/Game.ts src/core/BoardManager.ts

# Start development
npm run dev
```

This rule set ensures consistent, maintainable, and performant PixiJS v8 development across all projects. 